{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DTzgG5C5qv5qLeq3vTstL2","type":"tool_result","content":"*   **KP Links:** The `relevant_kps` need to be formatted into valid markdown links. Assume a standard URL structure (e.g., `.../kps/{kp_id}`).\r\n\r\n\r\n## Iteration 11 - Story: BEV Diagnostic Fault Code Scenario Generator (US-037)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- fault-code-scenarios.json: 20 BEV fault codes in compact single-line-per-entry JSON format\r\n- generate-scenarios.py: load_fault_codes() and create_scenario_question() with CLI (--list, --output, --out-dir)\r\n- tests/test_fault_scenarios.py: 6 tests covering count, schema, KP links, system coverage, format, CLI\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- Compact JSON (one object per line) keeps data files under 25 lines vs 300+ with pretty-print\r\n- For hyphenated filenames, use importlib.util.spec_from_file_location() to import in tests\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- Previous attempt produced 4697-line diff; reduced to ~210 by using compact JSON format\r\n- Python files with hyphens in name can't be imported via sys.path — need importlib workaround\r\n## Iteration 2 - Fri, Apr 17, 2026 12:46:10 PM\r\nCompleted: BEV Diagnostic Fault Code Scenario Generator (ID: US-037) in 6m\r\n\r\n## Iteration 1 - Fri, Apr 17, 2026 12:47:55 PM\r\nFAILED diagnosis-block gate: BEV Diagnostic Fault Code Scenario Generator (ID: US-037) — no diagnosis block found — attempt 1/3\r\n\r\n\r\n## Pre-analysis for US-037 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\r\nThis is a Python-based content generation task, not a Frappe integration. The context of `lhdn_payroll_integration` should be disregarded as it contradicts the user story's technical details.\r\n\r\n**Technical Brief: US-037 - BEV Diagnostic Fault Code Scenario Generator**\r\n\r\n**1. Python Files to Modify/Create:**\r\n*   `bev-diagnostic-rectification/_tools/generate-scenarios.py` (New File): This is the primary implementation file. It should contain the core logic.\r\n    *   `load_fault_codes(path)`: Function to load and parse the source JSON.\r\n    *   `create_scenario_question(data)`: Function to format a single fault code into a markdown string.\r\n*   `bev-diagnostic-rectification/_tools/fault-code-scenarios.json` (New File): A data file to be populated with 20+ BEV fault codes according to the specified structure.\r\n*   `tests/test_fault_scenarios.py` (Existing/New): A test file to validate the generator's output, specifically checking for correct Knowledge Point (KP) linking.\r\n\r\n**2. Frappe DocTypes/Hooks Involved:**\r\n*   None. This is a standalone Python script executed via `uv run`. The implementation requires no interaction with the Frappe framework.\r\n\r\n**3. Recommended Implementation Approach:**\r\n1.  Create the `generate-scenarios.py` script with placeholder functions.\r\n2.  Develop the logic to read a JSON file and loop through its entries.\r\n3.  Use a template or f-string to format each entry into the required KT markdown structure.\r\n4.  For the `fault-code-scenarios.json` file, create it with a small sample (2-3 codes) first to test the script, then populate it fully as a separate step.\r\n\r\n**4. Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\r\n*   **Previous Failure:** The last attempt failed due to an \"oversized_diff\". **Do not generate the script and the large JSON data file in the same operation.** Create the Python script first, then create the `fault-code-scenarios.json` data file in a subsequent, separate step to keep changes small.\r\n*   **File Paths:** Avoid hardcoding paths. Use `pathlib` and consider command-line arguments (`argparse`) for the input JSON and output directory.\r\n*   **KP Links:** The `relevant_kps` need to be formatted into valid markdown links. Assume a standard URL structure (e.g., `.../kps/{kp_id}`).\r\n\r\n\r\n## Iteration 12 - Thu, Apr 17, 2026\r\nCompleted: BEV Diagnostic Fault Code Scenario Generator (ID: US-037) — attempt 2, verified existing implementation\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- Previous attempt already created all files (committed in 66a680d)\r\n- This attempt: verified tests pass (6/6), CLI works, marked passes: true\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- Diagnosis block MUST be output before any file edits — gate enforced by ralph.sh\r\n- When implementation exists from prior commits, verify before re-implementing\r\n## Iteration 2 - Fri, Apr 17, 2026 12:52:41 PM\r\nCompleted: BEV Diagnostic Fault Code Scenario Generator (ID: US-037) in 3m\r\n\r\n## Iteration 3 - Fri, Apr 17, 2026 12:54:39 PM\nCompleted: Create KT Question Diversity Analyzer with Question Type Distribution Metrics and Recommendations (ID: US-027) in 7m\n\n\n## Iteration 13 - Story: KK Safety Checkpoint Validator (US-028)\n\n### What was implemented\n- validators/kk_safety_checkpoint_validator.py: scans KK-*.md files for missing safety checkpoints\n- REQUIRED_CHECKPOINTS dict: BEV (ppe_verification, insulation_test, ground_continuity, hv_isolation, lockout_tagout), Aesthetic (hygiene, contraindication_screening, client_comfort, patch_test, equipment_sterilisation)\n- SAFETY_RISK_MAP: CRITICAL/HIGH/MEDIUM per checkpoint; NOSS_REFS for each\n- audit_kk_file() checks full file text for keyword presence per checkpoint\n- generate_report() outputs HTML table with risk level and NOSS reference per gap\n- tests/test_kk_safety_validator.py: 7 tests, seeded bare BEV KK (5 gaps) + partial Aesthetic KK (3 gaps) = 8+ total\n\n### Patterns discovered\n- Keyword presence search in full file text (not per-step) is simpler and sufficient for checkpoint detection\n- HTML report format matches question_diversity_analyzer.py pattern (table with headers)\n- `detect_subject()` infers subject from path string (bev/g452 vs aesthetic/s960)\n\n### Gotchas\n- Seeded test KK content must not contain any of the checkpoint keywords to get reliable gap counts\n- Windows CRLF warning on git add is harmless — git handles line endings correctly\n\n## Iteration 4 - Thu, Apr 17, 2026\nCompleted: KK Step-by-Step Safety Validator with Checkpoint Auditing and Gap Flagging (ID: US-028) — verified existing implementation\n\n### What was implemented\n- validators/kk_safety_checkpoint_validator.py: REQUIRED_CHECKPOINTS (BEV+Aesthetic), SAFETY_RISK_MAP, NOSS_REFS, audit_kk_file(), scan_all_kk(), generate_report() with HTML output\n- tests/test_kk_safety_validator.py: 7 tests, all passing including integration test for 8+ missing checkpoints\n\n### Patterns discovered\n- When prior commit already contains the implementation, verify tests pass first before touching any files\n- BEV bare KK (5 checkpoints missing) + Aesthetic partial KK (3 missing) = 8 total, meeting the >=8 criterion\n## Iteration 3 - Fri, Apr 17, 2026 12:57:43 PM\nCompleted: Create KK Step-by-Step Safety Validator with Checkpoint Auditing and Gap Flagging (ID: US-028) in 3m","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"39c56169-26c0-472a-94b4-c164c63a4f53","uuid":"06d8a7f3-bb71-4ba8-9957-cc066f71020a","timestamp":"2026-04-17T04:58:34.874Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"*   **KP Links:** The `relevant_kps` need to be formatted into valid markdown links. Assume a standard URL structure (e.g., `.../kps/{kp_id}`).\r\n\r\n\r\n## Iteration 11 - Story: BEV Diagnostic Fault Code Scenario Generator (US-037)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- fault-code-scenarios.json: 20 BEV fault codes in compact single-line-per-entry JSON format\r\n- generate-scenarios.py: load_fault_codes() and create_scenario_question() with CLI (--list, --output, --out-dir)\r\n- tests/test_fault_scenarios.py: 6 tests covering count, schema, KP links, system coverage, format, CLI\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- Compact JSON (one object per line) keeps data files under 25 lines vs 300+ with pretty-print\r\n- For hyphenated filenames, use importlib.util.spec_from_file_location() to import in tests\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- Previous attempt produced 4697-line diff; reduced to ~210 by using compact JSON format\r\n- Python fi