{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VMbKh7zrzGH4qkxxwogRqv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# PENILAIAN PENGETAHUAN / KNOWLEDGE ASSESSMENT\n2\t\n3\t**Kod WIM / WIM Code:** G452-010-3:2023-C01/KA\n4\t**Kertas Warna / Paper Color:** MERAH JAMBU / PINK\n5\t\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t## Competency Unit: Perform BEV Scheduled Maintenance (G452-010-3:2023-C01)\n9\t\n10\t| Field | Detail |\n11\t|-------|--------|\n12\t| Duration | 1 hour 30 minutes |\n13\t| Total Marks | 100 |\n14\t| Passing Mark | 60% (60 marks) |\n15\t| References Covered | KP(1/3), KP(2/3), KP(3/3) |\n16\t\n17\t---\n18\t\n19\t## Instructions to Candidates\n20\t\n21\t1. This assessment consists of THREE (3) sections: A, B, and C\n22\t2. Answer ALL questions in ALL sections\n23\t3. Write your answers in the spaces provided or on the answer sheet\n24\t4. Marks for each question are indicated in brackets\n25\t\n26\t---\n27\t\n28\t## SECTION A: Multiple Choice Questions (20 marks)\n29\t\n30\tChoose the BEST answer for each question. Each question carries 2 marks.\n31\t\n32\t**A1.** Which Act governs occupational safety and health in a BEV maintenance workshop in Malaysia?\n33\t- A. Employment Act 1955\n34\t- B. Occupational Safety and Health Act 1994\n35\t- C. Road Transport Act 1987\n36\t- D. Factories and Machinery Act 1967\n37\t\n38\t**A2.** What is the minimum rated voltage for insulated gloves used in BEV HV work (Class 0)?\n39\t- A. 500V AC\n40\t- B. 750V AC\n41\t- C. 1000V AC\n42\t- D. 7500V AC\n43\t\n44\t**A3.** What type of fire extinguisher is required for lithium battery fires?\n45\t- A. Class A (water)\n46\t- B. Class B (foam)\n47\t- C. Class C (CO2)\n48\t- D. Class D (dry powder for metal fires)\n49\t\n50\t**A4.** What is the function of the Insulation Monitoring Device (IMD) in a BEV?"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"39c56169-26c0-472a-94b4-c164c63a4f53","uuid":"c157e50f-ee1e-4136-b194-e8b1c648f5cf","timestamp":"2026-04-17T04:59:27.316Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\bev-diagnostic-rectification\\C01\\KA.md","content":"# PENILAIAN PENGETAHUAN / KNOWLEDGE ASSESSMENT\n\n**Kod WIM / WIM Code:** G452-010-3:2023-C01/KA\n**Kertas Warna / Paper Color:** MERAH JAMBU / PINK\n\n---\n\n## Competency Unit: Perform BEV Scheduled Maintenance (G452-010-3:2023-C01)\n\n| Field | Detail |\n|-------|--------|\n| Duration | 1 hour 30 minutes |\n| Total Marks | 100 |\n| Passing Mark | 60% (60 marks) |\n| References Covered | KP(1/3), KP(2/3), KP(3/3) |\n\n---\n\n## Instructions to Candidates\n\n1. This assessment consists of THREE (3) sections: A, B, and C\n2. Answer ALL questions in ALL sections\n3. Write your answers in the spaces provided or on the answer sheet\n4. Marks for each question are indicated in brackets\n\n---\n\n## SECTION A: Multiple Choice Questions (20 marks)\n\nChoose the BEST answer for each question. Each question carries 2 marks.\n\n**A1.** Which Act governs occupational safety and health in a BEV maintenance workshop in Malaysia?\n- A. Employment Act 1955\n- B. Occupational Safety and Health Act 1994\n- C. Road Transport Act 1987\n- D. Factories and Machinery Act 1967\n\n**A2.** What is the minimum rated voltage for insulated gloves used in BEV HV work (Class 0)?\n- A. 500V AC\n- B. 750V AC\n- C. 1000V AC\n- D. 7500V AC\n\n**A3.** What type of fire extinguisher is required for lithium battery fires?\n- A. Class A (water)\n- B. Class B (foam)\n- C. Class C (CO2)\n- D. Class D (dry powder for metal fires)\n\n**A4.** What is the function of the Insulation Monitoring Device (IMD) in a BEV?","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":321}}}
